theory/lanes/blitz-2026-08-29/bta-probe/lane.log:1833:| A-INDEX-PEPS | Conditional selection theorem (the single categorical hybrid row; FUSION-SOFT is its linear Fourier/window corollary, not a second row): under the displayed PEPS typing hypotheses (PT1)--(PT3) of theory/anyon-label-index.md §5 (with (PT4) only for the instrument-normalization clause), on the finite annular register `P_b T_{(x,mu)} P_a = 0` unless `mu ∈ Hom(b, x⊗a)` and `N_{xa}^b > 0`; the same-circle instrument weight is supported on allowed fusion events, and the windowed/momentum form `P_b T_x(k;w) P_a` obeys the same selection in the declared topology of the hybrid §2.  Invertible `x` gives an `Inv(Z(𝒞))` index; general `x` gives only the universal-grading shadow.  NOT claimed: any microscopic pure-endpoint/instrument instantiation beyond toric code (open obligation), any Taylor coefficient inside an allowed channel (NO-CAT-SOFT fence), any packaging of the three mechanisms under one theorem. | **PROVED** (conditional implication on (PT1)--(PT3); promoted per w21-joint-critic.md §9 item 5 after the Lamport repair, orchestrator-verified) | A-INDEX-TC-fin | theory/anyon-selection-hybrid.md ⟨1⟩1 | theory/checks/anyon_label_check.py ANYON-C0--C4; theory/checks/cat_hunt_check.py CATH-C0--C4; theory/checks/soft_2d_hunt_check.py S2DH gates |
