theory/verdicts/w21-joint-critic.md:99:**(b) Independent computation.**  The proof fixes the categorical/channel/support/homogeneous-equation data and replaces the endpoint family by `c(k)T_x(k)`.  With `c(k)=exp(i alpha k^n)`, the zero-momentum operator and all lower jets are fixed while the `n`th derivative changes by `i alpha n! T_x(0)`.  On the patch, changing `lambda` changes the probe: the phase slope is `1.000i` versus `2.750i`; path-curvature and projected-rotation-curvature ratios are both `4.000000`.  These are genuine operator families in one toric-code Hamiltonian, but they do not keep a complete microscopic source protocol fixed while varying only the model.  This is the same distinction enforced in `theory/amp.md`: a relation-level witness proves underdetermination by the listed relations, not physical nonuniversality over a fully specified model class.
