1157:This works as the condition $S_q(A^{ab})=\exp(i\phi(q))X_q^\dagger A^{ab} X_q$ is equivalent to the 2-cocycle equation. This MPS has zero correlation length (which follows from the fact that the transfer matrix is a rank 1 projector) and hence represents the renormalization group fixed point in its corresponding phase.  In the particular case of e.g.\ an on-site $Z_2\times Z_2$ symmetry, the simplest group exhibiting non-trivial 2-cocycles, this construction precisely yields the 1D cluster state (Appendix \ref{app:examples}) when blocking pairs of adjacent sites.
