2480:The quantum double description for a group $G$ as discussed in the previous section is a special case of this string net representations. The two options discussed above correspond to $\mathcal{D}=\mathcal{M}=\mathcal{C}=\mathrm{Vec}_{G}$ and to $\mathcal{D}=\mathrm{Vec}_{G},\,\mathcal{M}=\mathrm{Vec},\,\mathcal{C}=\mathrm{Rep}(G)$. Additionally, one can define two more Morita equivalent PEPS with physical labels in $\mathrm{Rep}(G)$ as $\mathcal{D}=\mathcal{M}=\mathcal{C}=\mathrm{Rep}(G)$ or as $\mathcal{D}=\mathrm{Rep}(G),\,\mathcal{M}=\mathrm{Vec},\,\mathcal{C}=\mathrm{Vec}_G$. Here, $\mathrm{Vec}_G$ is the category with the group elements as labels, and $\mathrm{Vec}$ is the trivial category consisting out of only 1 element.
